/backend/target
# Rust build output wherever a crate lives. `/backend/target` above covered the
# only crate there was; `pos-desktop/src-tauri` grew one and 2.047 files of
# `target/debug/deps` nearly went into a commit.
**/target/
.env
*.log
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
semantic-review/
**/semantic-review/

# Edge runtime databases. A shop's SQLite file is state, not source: committing
# one puts a snapshot of somebody's stock — and its write-ahead log — into every
# clone, and the next person to run a server overwrites it in their diff.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal

# The demo DC node runs from its own directory with its own .env and SQLite.
demo/

# The Android till builds into its own tree. Gradle's outputs are hundreds of
# megabytes of dex, merged jars and signed APKs — a rebuild reproduces every
# one of them, and none of them belong in a clone. `local.properties` is the
# SDK path on whoever's laptop ran the build, which is never the next one's.
tablet/.gradle/
tablet/build/
tablet/app/build/
tablet/local.properties

# Its own git repository (685 MB of it). Staging it produces a gitlink nobody
# can clone, not the files.
/rfid-homepage/

# rig run environments (DBs live in Postgres as sim_rig_*, files here)
runs/

# Local demo environment (store back-office demo): DBs, binaries, credentials.
.demo/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Third-party repositories cloned for research
research/erpnext-indonesia/agile-technica/
research/erpnext-indonesia/andrimuhyidin/
